:2.620658949243099,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":30.7,"_gate_accruals":-0.08176714669270198,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":81.7,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.8695371510627835,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.03005000687023103,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":62.4,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.009002052012028167,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":3.342435440127903,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.09927793398823839,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":49.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.008259818924005097,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":30.6,"_gate_pool_share":-0.012386938124418823,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":35.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.006790977348149818,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":28.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.017301507392666116,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":16.3,"_gate_margins":0.1066031195430884,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":100.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.03535830374500002,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":35.4,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.005564438904787028,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":17.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0034543137247691202,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":45.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009439745004290793,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.02157,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["flagged"],"description_full":"XPO, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides freight transportation services in the United States, North America, France, the United Kingdom, and rest of Europe. The company operates in two segments, North American Less-Than-Truckload (LTL) and European Transportation. The North American LTL segment provides shippers with geographic density and day-definite domestic and cross-border services to the U.S., Mexico, Canada, and the Caribbean. The European Transportation segment offers dedicated truckload, LTL, truck brokerage, managed transportation, last mile, freight forwarding, and warehousing and multimodal solutions to an extensive base of customers within the consumer, trade, and industrial markets. The company was formerly known as XPO Logistics, Inc. and changed its name to XPO, Inc. in December 2022. The company was founded in 1989 and is based in Greenwich, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mario A. Harik | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 44 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 38K people. Revenue per employee of $215K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 31%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["XPO, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $22.5B market cap on $8.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $329M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 91% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.914971567831988},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"One of 3 ratings agencies now has XPO as investment-grade","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/